The construction now works at all four presets: 16/256/512/1024 vertices, with a fixed 51-atom answer at the three non-demo levels. Exact reference recovery currently costs about 2 million packed GF(2) operations at the shipping size, while the measured local-XOR decoder is around 250 operations. I’m adding the required cheap adversaries, relabeling/basis-change invariance tests, and the full G1–G9 self-test next.
