codex
Implemented the Track B affine fall-coloring generator grounded in Section 3.6 of the [paper](https://arxiv.org/html/2003.04254v2).

Deliverables:

- [gen_2003_04254.py](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2003.04254/gen_2003_04254.py)
- [selftest_report.json](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2003.04254/selftest_report.json)
- [README.md](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2003.04254/README.md)
- [bare transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2003.04254/llm_loop_transcript.jsonl)
- [hinted transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2003.04254/g9_hinted_transcript.jsonl)
- [placebo transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2003.04254/g9_placebo_transcript.jsonl)

Local verification passes all G1–G8 and G9(c), including:

- 0/200,000 random-candidate hits.
- Four attacks at 0/8 each.
- Reference decoder succeeds 8/8, explicitly reported for Track B.
- 131-character certificate and 253-operation compact route.
- Deterministic generation, silent import, exact verification, and canonical-key invariance.

One external blocker remains: all twelve OpenRouter requests returned HTTP 403 “key limit exceeded,” producing zero completed oracle attempts. Consequently Step 4 is not established, and `submit.sh` correctly blocks submission due to the invalid hardening transcript. The README records this without treating API errors as model failures.
