14:## Problem and trust model
20:## Why Track B
24:For this distribution, a construction-specific polynomial algorithm exists and is disclosed: recover the cover fibers from the nullspace of adjacency-plus-identity over GF(2), then fit an affine projection. Packed exact Gaussian elimination costs `O(n^3/word_size)`. On eight shipping instances it solved 8/8 in 1.143 seconds and 15,757,327 packed exact operations, at most 1,978,355 on one instance. The compact route notices that the XOR of the eight coordinates in a closed neighborhood is killed by the coloring matrix; a handful of these signatures exposes its three-dimensional kernel. The measured compact route uses at most 253 packed exact operations. The benchmark tests whether a no-tool solver finds that invariant, not whether the instances defeat software.
26:## Worked demo
90:## Difficulty and gates
95:| easy | 256 | 16 | 896 | 51 | locally verified; oracle unavailable |
96:| medium | 512 | 16 | 1,792 | 51 | locally verified; oracle unavailable |
108:| G8 | 100 relabeling invariance checks, 120 witness transports, and 20/20 distinct unrelated keys |
111:## Oracle loop and G9 diagnostics
113:The required harness was run, but OpenRouter rejected every request with HTTP 403 `Key limit exceeded (total limit)`. By design, API errors do not consume attempts and are not evidence that a model failed. Therefore the candidate has **not** cleared the four-vendor hardening loop and must not be represented as oracle-hardened until the harness is rerun with quota.
117:| bare | easy | 0 | 4 | no verdict; quota blocked the run |
123:## Use
135:From the repository root, after a successful oracle rerun:
143:## Caveats
145:The family is easy with exact GF(2) elimination, and the displayed coordinates intentionally create the compact invariant; this is the Track B premise, not hidden hardness. The 0/200,000 guess result estimates only the declared prior of ordered full-rank affine maps with uniform offsets; it is not a proof of solution density and says nothing about informed candidates. The adversary panel did not test general-purpose SAT/SMT, integer programming, Weisfeiler-Leman refinement, or every spectral clustering variant. The reference nullspace decoder is construction-specific and succeeds. Canonicalization is exact for vertex renumbering, edge reordering, affine coordinate changes, and their compositions, but it is not a complete graph-isomorphism canonical form. Most importantly, no LLM hardness conclusion is currently justified because all oracle and G9 calls failed before model inference.

