README.md:24:For this distribution, a construction-specific polynomial algorithm exists and is disclosed: recover the cover fibers from the nullspace of adjacency-plus-identity over GF(2), then fit an affine projection. Packed exact Gaussian elimination costs `O(n^3/word_size)`. On eight shipping instances it solved 8/8 in 1.143 seconds and 15,757,327 packed exact operations, at most 1,978,355 on one instance. The compact route notices that the XOR of the eight coordinates in a closed neighborhood is killed by the coloring matrix; a handful of these signatures exposes its three-dimensional kernel. The measured compact route uses at most 253 packed exact operations. The benchmark tests whether a no-tool solver finds that invariant, not whether the instances defeat software.
